      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Starting at age 35 is absolutely doable, and a 4-week linear progression plan focusing on squats, bench presses, and deadlifts is a fantastic way to build a foundational strength base safely. Since you are new to lifting, begin with moderate weights that allow you to perform repetitions with perfect form before adding load in the following week. Your workouts should include 3 days of rest between leg sessions and rotating chest/back days for the bench and deadlifts to ensure adequate recovery. Stick strictly to the weight increase increments—such as 2.5% of your set weight—and rest 3–5 minutes between heavy sets to prioritize safety over intensity. If you feel any sharp pain or excessive fatigue, stop immediately and consult a coach or physician before continuing.",
