      "content": "Here is a specific 4-week split: Week 1 starts with light weights and high reps (20 min) to learn form; Week 2 adds 2.5 lbs per set; Week 3 increases effort toward 12 reps before Week 4 performs your first overhead squat and heavy deadlift attempt. You should rest 48 hours between heavy compound sessions to prevent injury. To handle soreness, incorporate 5 minutes of stretching daily and try to sleep 7–9 hours to allow your muscles to recover properly. Listen to your body—if pain feels sharp or persistent, scale back immediately, but general muscle burn is normal and indicates good progress. Consistency over 4 weeks will lay a solid foundation for your future training.",
